(SOP-REV-003: Report Review and Closure Approval) Tj T*
(Version: 1.0) Tj T*
(Effective Date: 2025-09-01) Tj T*
(Status: Active) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Purpose) Tj T*
(This fictional training SOP explains how a report moves from NEW to IN_REVIEW and finally to) Tj T*
(CLOSED.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Status lifecycle) Tj T*
(2.1 Allowed transitions) Tj T*
(A report moves from NEW to IN_REVIEW when a reviewer starts work. A report moves from) Tj T*
(IN_REVIEW to CLOSED only after a documented human approval.) Tj T*
(WARNING: A report must never move directly from NEW to CLOSED. A closed report cannot be) Tj T*
(reopened in this prototype.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Closure approval) Tj T*
(3.1 Requesting closure) Tj T*
(The intake operator or reviewer submits a closure request for a report that is IN_REVIEW. The) Tj T*
(request records who asked and the record version at the time.) Tj T*
(3.2 Approving closure) Tj T*
(A different human reviewer approves the request. The person who requested closure cannot) Tj T*
(approve it. Software agents and AI assistants can never approve closure.) Tj T*
(EXCEPTION: If the record changed after the request was made, the approval is rejected and) Tj T*
(closure must be requested again.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Audit) Tj T*
(Every status change and approval is written to the audit trail with the actor, timestamp and) Tj T*
(outcome.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
